{
  "id": "V04",
  "title": "Aspect ratio factor and walls over 3.5",
  "intent": "Four walls at one 7 ft story with h/b = 2.0, 2.5, 3.5 and 4.0. Proves the SDPWS 2021 aspect ratio factor C_hb = 1.25 − 0.125·h/b for 2 < h/b ≤ 3.5, that it scales both the capacity and the capacity-distribution weight, and that a wall over 3.5 is flagged (aspect_ratio warning) and takes no shear.",
  "covers": [
    "SDPWS 2021 §4.3.4 aspect ratio",
    "SDPWS 4.3.3.4.1 capacity distribution with C_hb",
    "aspect_ratio audit warning",
    "G2 / G11"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Story shear V = 3 k, h = 7 ft. Walls: SW-1 L = 3.5 ft, h/b = 7/3.5 = 2.00; SW-2 L = 2.8 ft, h/b = 7/2.8 = 2.50; SW-3 L = 2 ft, h/b = 7/2 = 3.50; SW-4 L = 1.75 ft, h/b = 7/1.75 = 4.00."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "C_hb: SW-1 h/b 2.00 ≤ 2 → 1.0; SW-2 1.25 − 0.125 × 2.5 = 0.9375; SW-3 1.25 − 0.125 × 3.5 = 0.8125; SW-4 h/b 4.00 > 3.5 → not a shear wall (C_hb = 0, no shear, audit warning)."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Reduced capacity at 6\" o.c. (312 plf): SW-1 312 × 1.0000 = 312.00 plf; SW-2 312 × 0.9375 = 292.50 plf; SW-3 312 × 0.8125 = 253.50 plf."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Weights v_cap × L: SW-1 312.00 × 3.5 = 1092.00 lb; SW-2 292.50 × 2.8 = 819.00 lb; SW-3 253.50 × 2 = 507.00 lb; Σ = 2418.00 lb (SW-4 0)."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Shares V × wt / Σ: SW-1 1.3548 k; SW-2 1.0161 k; SW-3 0.6290 k; SW-4 0 k. Unit shears 0.7·V/L: SW-1 270.97 plf; SW-2 254.03 plf; SW-3 220.16 plf — all ≤ their reduced 6\" capacity, so 6\" o.c. stays."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "D/C = v / (312·C_hb) = 0.8685 at every sheathed wall (the capacity method gives every wall the same D/C)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "SW-1 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 1.355 / 3.5 = 387.10 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0170; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1694; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 2709.68 / 3790 (ASD cap) = 0.0908 (HDUE3, T = 2709.68 lb); r = 2709.68 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.4129 → Δ_c = 0.0113; h·Δa/b = 7 × (0.0908 + 0.0113) / 3.5 = 0.2042 → δ = 0.3906 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "SW-2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 1.016 / 2.8 = 362.90 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0199; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1588; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 2540.32 / 3790 (ASD cap) = 0.0851 (HDUE3, T = 2540.32 lb); r = 2540.32 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.3871 → Δ_c = 0.0106; h·Δa/b = 7 × (0.0851 + 0.0106) / 2.8 = 0.2393 → δ = 0.4180 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "SW-3 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 0.629 / 2 = 314.52 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0242; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1376; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 2201.61 / 3790 (ASD cap) = 0.0738 (HDUE3, T = 2201.61 lb); r = 2201.61 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.3355 → Δ_c = 0.0092; h·Δa/b = 7 × (0.0738 + 0.0092) / 2 = 0.2904 → δ = 0.4522 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "SW-4 (h/b 4.00 > 3.5) is not a shear wall: no share, no deflection, not part of the story drift. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-3 0.4522 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.4522 / 1.0 = 1.809 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 7 × 12 = 1.680 in → NG — over the limit (design pinned, so drift sizing does not change it; the line reports drift NG). The short walls deflect most for their shear (the 8vh³/EAb and h·Δa/b terms grow with h/b): this case keeps its pinned design and verifies the drift NG."
    }
  ],
